Package: bluetui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, bluez
Description: lightweight nmtui-style TUI for Bluetooth
 bluetui is a small, fast terminal interface for managing Bluetooth on Linux,
 styled after NetworkManager's nmtui. It talks to BlueZ over D-Bus and lets
 you:
 .
  * toggle the adapter on/off and scan for devices;
  * connect, disconnect, pair and remove devices;
  * complete interactive pairing (PIN / passkey / confirmation) via a
    registered org.bluez.Agent1 agent.
 .
 The device list updates live from BlueZ signals and keeps connected and
 paired devices at the top.
